Magistrate (Central)("ADM" in short), New Delhi directing the appellant to pay a penalty of Rs.1,50,000/, under Section 51 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006("FSS Act" in short) for violation of Section 26(2)(ii) of FSS Act read with Section 3(1) (zx) of FSS Act for selling sub standard food/milk.
3.0 The appellant has challenged the impugned order inter alia on the grounds that:
(i) no independent witness was joined at the time of lifting of the sample in violation of Section 38(7) FSS Act;
M/s Priya Dutt Sharma vs State, Through Commissioner, Department of Food Safety & Ors.
(ii) Rule 2.4.1(7) of FSSR which requires that the sample food article has to be taken in clean and dry bottles/jar etc. was not complied with.
Thus,enquiry proceedings were not conducted properly;
(v) sanction is bad in law as it suffers from non M/s Priya Dutt Sharma vs State, Through Commissioner, Department of Food Safety & Ors.
